<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arechis I of Benevento</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 641</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arechis I was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> from 591 to 641, appointed after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zotto">Zotto</a>, the first duke. During his fifty-year rule he extended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> duchy over most of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, taking Capua and sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crotone">Crotone</a>, though he could not capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. He laid the foundations of a duchy largely independent of the Lombard kings at Pavia.</p></div>
